## Bounded implementation

The one existing `attachCallAction` method is now legal only while the
transaction is registering. It validates the complete already-registered
handle set before assigning `call_action`. A non-null `call_action` closes
registration and every other per-request attachment path. The resulting
order is:

```text
register all requests -> attach exactly once -> seal -> prepare
  -> materializeAll/action execution -> commit
```

A zero-handle direct action attaches before seal without a fake request.
Duplicate attachment remains `ValueUseCallActionAlreadyAttached`; attachment,
registration, or another per-request action after attachment is
`ValueUseLateRegistration`. The former sealed-only error was not repurposed
as another mechanism.

The private `CallFinalUsePin` adds only:

```text
plan_identity: usize
admission_position: usize
interval_end: usize
```

It is nested in the existing private lifetime pin and contains no `ValueLoc`,
slice, callback, mutable-plan pointer, physical-home capability, or public
accessor. Admission is limited to a current named request claimed by the
already attached `.direct_call` or `.int_byte_size_call` action. It requires
the exact predecessor boundary, the same real allocation plan, canonical
identity/generation, canonical dependencies, existing type/class/width/form/
destination compatibility, and the action's closed EAX/RAX home. Generic Q1
and forward Q1 are unchanged.

Canonical revalidation occurs during prepared-record construction, every
post-preservation call-argument refresh, and every argument stage. A plan,
position, interval, binding, generation, home, handle, or action-claim
change fails request-attributably before further emission. Q2 survival and
Q3 occupant preservation remain independent. `materializeAll` remains the
sole automatic rollback owner.

Attachment validation now records the first precise request failure for a
valid in-authority handle, source-order inversion, unexpected independent
request action, and an unclaimed registered request. Phase, tag, identity,
count, and foreign/no-matching-handle failures remain authority-level.

## Proof matrix

The frozen 57-case design matrix is covered by the existing call-action
matrix plus the following amended proof groups:

| design rows | proof |
|---|---|
| 1–9 | `value-use call final-use plan admits exact EAX and RAX argument positions`; `supports middle last repeated and specialized operands`; existing zero-argument/result-durability call tests |
| 10–15 | `value-use call final-use plan preserves Q2 source and unrelated Q3 occupant`; existing caller-clobber/multi-alias call tests |
| 16–32 | `value-use call final-use admission rejects incomplete and ineligible state`; `structural pin fails closed on canonical mutation`; existing forward-Q1, retained-form, handle, type/home, and dependency negatives |
| 33–44 | `value-use dormant call attachment is pre-seal unique and closes registration`; existing provenance, validation-order, phase, copy-cycle, and retained-form tests |
| 45–53 | exact-final-use positive and structural-mutation tests plus the existing complete call rollback matrix and later-index three-argument rollback proof |
| 54–57 | byte-identical production source hashes, decisive accepted-cohort identities, focused canaries, and dormant production guards |

The structural-pin mutation loop independently changes the allocation-plan
identity, current position, interval, binding presence, virtual generation,
and admitted home. Attachment tests explicitly pin registering phase,
zero-request state, successful attachment state, registration closure,
duplicate rejection, and cleared action/execution storage after rollback.
The transaction layout proof now pins size 366240, alignment 16, field order,
defaults, and every field offset.

## Structural guards

The authority guard freezes:

- registering-only attachment, validation-before-assignment, duplicate
  rejection, and registration closure;
- private inline final-use storage and exact predecessor arithmetic;
- direct-call/intByteSize handle claims and exact EAX/RAX admission;
- prepared-record, refresh, and per-stage canonical revalidation;
- no public final-use helper, retained raw location, liveness callback, or
  generic-Q1 widening.

The production guard is function/API scoped. A future ordinary wiring shape
is accepted only in `lowerCall`, the pure
`isAdmittedOrdinaryDirectCall` classifier, and
`lowerOrdinaryDirectCallValueUse`, with lexical register-before-attach-before-
seal ordering and one authority. Negative fixtures reject relocation,
attachment after seal, registration after attachment, duplicate attachment,
specialized premature wiring, and selector/home/liveness inspection. The
guard deliberately accepts `.direct_call` in an EFLAGS instruction-effect
fixture and does not impose an opcode-wide ban.

Failure-provenance accounting is conditional: a present memcpy mapper owns
exactly three query sites and a present direct-call mapper owns exactly one
per-handle-loop query site. A memcpy-only fixture is not required to invent a
call mapper.

